<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ioannis Malachias</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ioannis Malachias was a Greek doctor who led the uprising on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ikaria">Icaria</a> in July 1912, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italo-turkish-war">Italo-Turkish War</a>. The islanders forced the small Ottoman garrison to surrender and proclaimed the Free State of Icaria, with Malachias as its leading figure. The short-lived state lasted about five months until the island joined the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> in November 1912.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ioannis-malachias.jpg" alt="Ioannis Malachias" width="320" height="389" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%CE%99%CF%89%CE%AC%CE%BD%CE%BD%CE%B7%CF%82_%CE%9C%CE%B1%CE%BB%CE%B1%CF%87%CE%AF%CE%B1%CF%82.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
